 "reason": "The specification is a faithful, complete and correct formulation of the idea. Cohesion: A from adjacent training pairs only, D = ceil(mean full degree over all n_train items with isolated items at 0), N(i) = top-D neighbours with ascending-id tie-break, sim_ij = |N(i) cap N(j)|/sqrt(deg_i deg_j) in [0,1], coh_i = (1/deg_i) sum_{j in N(i)} sim_ij in [0,1], with the truncated-sum/full-degree normaliser of the idea kept and its degree confound declared rather than hidden. Rank: rho_i = (#{j in P: coh_j < coh_i} + 0.5 #{j in P: coh_j = coh_i, j < i})/(|P|-1), exactly the idea's counts and the idea's amended denominator, range [0,1] (max = (|P|-1-0.5(g-1))/(|P|-1), min 0 — re-derived and correct), 0.5 for edge-less items, |P| = 1 giving 0.5. Cost: s_k = sigmoid(alpha_k) initialised at logit((k+0.5)/256), O_ik = beta R_c (1-|rho_i - s_k|) with R_c = 1/sqrt(c) = 1 and beta = m/R_c = m, m the median of d_c(x_i, y_{k1(i)}) measured once with O = 0 and frozen, C_ik = D_k - O_ik. Assignment: C is handed once to the baseline's own sinkhorn, which exponentiates it itself with sk_epsilon (no second exponentiation, no centring, no rescaling), the same row sums 1 and column sums B/K1, and k1 is the plan's argmax. Estimator: p_i = one_hot(k1_i) + P_i - P_i.detach() is algebraically the framework's canonical x + (x_q - x).detach() with x = P, forward value a_{k1}, and d/dP = 1 so the reconstruction gradient reaches alpha_k through P <- C <- |rho_i - s_k| <- sigmoid(alpha_k); the estimator is correctly described as a consequence of the differentiable plan, not as a third change, in agreement with the idea's 'the STE is the baseline's'. Reconstruction and residual recursion use the raw unlifted codeword while the cost uses exp_0^c(q_k); levels 2-3, the loss, the optimiser and the residual recursion are the baseline's. Geometry: the Mobius sum substitutes X = -x so the 2c<.,.> terms are negated, (-x)(+)y = ((1-2c<x,y>+c||y||^2)(-x)+(1-c||x||^2)y)/(1-2c<x,y>+c^2||x||^2||y||^2+eps); the symbolic statements (xy = -<x,y>, num0 = (1+2c*xy+c*yn)(-x0)+(1-c*xn)y0, same denominator) and the executable (generic +2c Mobius called as mobius(-x,y,c)) agree exactly, d_c(x,x) = 0, d_c(0,y) = (2/sqrt(c))artanh(sqrt(c)||y||), the numeric check at x=(0.1,0), y=(0,0.1), c=1 reproduces (1/sqrt(c))arcosh(1+2c||x-y||^2/((1-c||x||^2)(1-c||y||^2))), and the c->0 limit is 2||x-y||; the sign error that would return 0 at y = -x with limit 2||x+y|| is explicitly excluded. Switches: BEHAVIOUR_OFF makes the offset identically 0 so C_ik = D_k with curvature, strata code path and balanced plan intact; GEOMETRY_OFF sets c = 0 (identity lift, 2||x-y||) while keeping the frozen R_c = 1 and the curved arm's beta un-re-measured, so the two arms differ only in the distance, as the idea requires. The rho buffer is float32 [24556] indexed by global item id, train split only, and no validation/test behaviour enters it. The earlier defects (a stray tau in the operative surface, the estimator counted as a third change, and a curvature argument that did not match the pinned c) are repaired in this version, and I find no remaining gap, ambiguity, sign/scale/limit error or unstated gradient path."
